{"article": "Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better", "organization": "developers at Valve", "published_on": "2023-11-09T18:00:38+00:00", "passage": "Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better (Engadget, 2023-11-09T18:00:38+00:00)
The first thing to know about the Steam Deck OLED is that it’s not the Steam Deck 2. The Steam Deck OLED is a mid-cycle refresh from Valve, similar to the Switch OLED upgrade, but there’s a lot more going on internally here. Its screen is better, its battery life is better, its thumbsticks are better, the haptics are better, and its chip and thermals are better. One thing that hasn’t changed is its form factor — this is still one of the biggest babies on the handheld block.

The new Steam Deck’s main upgrade is its OLED screen, which replaces the original LCD and, crucially, has native support for HDR and faster frame rates. The OLED also has smaller bezels, making the display larger at 7.4 inches, compared with the original 7-inch screen."}

{"title":"The Steam Deck OLED arrives November 16 with an improved screen and longer battery life (Engadget, 2023-11-09T18:00:32+00:00)","text":"The Steam Deck OLED arrives November 16 with an improved screen and longer battery life (Engadget, 2023-11-09T18:00:32+00:00)
When asked about the potential for future hardware — like a return of the Steam Machine or an updated Steam Controller — there were no firm updates, but there does seem to be something happening. Griffais agreed that enabling the Steam Deck to work as a hybrid living room console was a "side goal" of the team, and noted that everything Valve does to improve SteamOS will benefit other devices. Coomer added that Valve is still working internally on "a bunch of controllers and prototypes." If SteamOS is being used on larger displays, the team would want to augment that experience with better input options. "We don't have any announcements on that front, but it's why we're building prototypes and thinking about the future there," Coomer said.

The Steam Deck OLED will be available to order on November 16th at 1PM ET. Valve expects units to begin shipping as soon as orders start to roll in. The updated pricing on the existing LCD models is already in effect.","entities":["Valve","Steam Deck","Steam Deck OLED","The Steam Deck OLED arrives November 16 with an improved screen and longer battery life","Steam Machine","Steam Controller","Griffais","SteamOS","Coomer","Engadget"],"facts":["Tim Sweeney on Epic’s victory royale over Google -MENTIONS-> Valve","The best October Prime Day gaming deals -MENTIONS-> Valve","The Epic v. Google trial may come down to simple v. complicated -MENTIONS-> Valve","The Steam Deck OLED improves much more than its screen -MENTIONS-> Valve","Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better -MENTIONS-> Valve"]}

{"title":"Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better (Engadget, 2023-11-09T18:00:38+00:00)","text":"Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better (Engadget, 2023-11-09T18:00:38+00:00)
The HDR OLED model is what they would have released the first time around, if the technology had existed before 2022. The handheld market has evolved quickly — in just over a year, the Steam Deck proved there’s widespread demand for handheld PCs, and its success helped drive chip makers and display manufacturers to build hardware specifically for high-fidelity mobile play. This is great news for Valve and the Steam Deck, and also the other handhelds coming out of companies like Ayaneo, ASUS, Ayn, Logitech, Retroid and Razer. Hell, maybe even Playdate will get an HDR OLED display one day. (Just kidding; Playdate is literally perfect).

So, no, the HDR OLED refresh isn't the Steam Deck 2, but it is a welcome improvement on an already good device. The Steam Deck OLED is the facetuned, photoshopped, spit-shined version of Valve’s handheld, and it features tangible, clever improvements.","entities":["HDR OLED display","Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better","Ayaneo","Ayn","Retroid","Playdate","handheld market","handheld PCs","high-fidelity mobile play","Steam Deck 2","Valve","Razer","Steam Deck","Asus","Steam Deck OLED"],"facts":["Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better -MENTIONS-> OLED screen","Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better -MENTIONS-> Sony","Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better -MENTIONS-> HDR","Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better -MENTIONS-> Switch OLED upgrade","Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better -MENTIONS-> LCD"]}

{"title":"The Steam Deck OLED arrives November 16 with an improved screen and longer battery life (Engadget, 2023-11-09T18:00:32+00:00)","text":"The Steam Deck OLED arrives November 16 with an improved screen and longer battery life (Engadget, 2023-11-09T18:00:32+00:00)
The original Steam Deck had a 7-inch 800p LCD running at 60Hz. The new model squeezes a 7.4-inch OLED screen into the same space, significantly shrinking the bezels around the display. The new panel runs at the same resolution, but with a refresh rate of up to 90Hz. It’s also HDR, covering 110 percent of the P3 color space with a peak brightness of 1,000 nits — the old model maxed out at around 400 nits. Like all OLED screens, it has pure blacks and near-instantaneous response times. As before, anti-glare etched glass is available, but only on the premium model.

The Steam Deck OLED has a die-shrunk version of the same custom APU found in the original Steam Deck. The new APU is produced on a 6nm process, rather than the older 7nm process.","entities":["Steam Deck","Steam Deck OLED","Steam Deck OLED arrival","The Steam Deck OLED arrives November 16 with an improved screen and longer battery life","Engadget"],"facts":["Steam Deck OLED review: It's just better -MENTIONS-> Steam Deck","Tim Sweeney on Epic’s victory royale over Google -MENTIONS-> Steam Deck","The best video games of the year so far -MENTIONS-> Steam Deck","The 53 best Black Friday deals we could find at Amazon, Walmart, Target and more -MENTIONS-> Steam Deck","The best Black Friday deals you can get for under $25 -MENTIONS-> Steam Deck"]}

{"title":"Amazon sellers sound off on the FTC's 'long-overdue' antitrust case (Cnbc | World Business News Leader, 2023-10-06T21:31:00+00:00)","text":"Amazon sellers sound off on the FTC's 'long-overdue' antitrust case (Cnbc | World Business News Leader, 2023-10-06T21:31:00+00:00)
Fred Ruckel

Nearly three years later, Ruckel’s experience hits at the core of a sweeping antitrust lawsuit filed last week by the Federal Trade Commission against Amazon. The agency accused Amazon of wielding its monopoly power to squeeze merchants and thwart rivals. For consumers, that’s led to artificially inflated prices and a degraded shopping experience, the agency alleges. In the 172-page suit, the FTC said Amazon relies on an “anti-discounting strategy” and a “massive web-crawling apparatus that constantly tracks online prices” to stifle competition. The agency said Amazon punishes third-party sellers who offer cheaper products elsewhere by threatening to disqualify them from appearing in the buy box if it detects a lower price. Losing the buy box is an “existential threat” to sellers’ businesses, the complaint alleges. The end result of these tactics, the FTC argues, is elevated prices across the web.","entities":["Federal Trade Commission","Fred Ruckel","sweeping antitrust lawsuit","monopoly power","Amazon sellers sound off on the FTC's 'long-overdue' antitrust case","CNBC","Amazon"],"facts":["5 things we learned so far about the Google antitrust case -MENTIONS-> monopoly power","Amazon sellers sound off on the FTC's 'long-overdue' antitrust case -MENTIONS-> Eastvale","Federal Trade Commission -PARTICIPATED_IN-> antitrust lawsuit against Amazon","ASX set to drop as Wall Street’s September slump deepens -MENTIONS-> Federal Trade Commission","Amazon sellers sound off on the FTC's 'long-overdue' antitrust case -MENTIONS-> Watchara Phomicinda"]}

